model_output_raw:
Okay, let's see. The user wants code for a login page. First, I need to figure out the structure. Usually, a login form has an input field for username and password, maybe a submit button. Then there's a section for the login credentials.

Wait, but maybe they're okay with just the form. So, I can start with the HTML. The form should have two input fields: one for username, another for password. The submit button would be next to them. Then, I can add some basic styling using CSS to make it look good. Maybe a border around the form and some padding to make it feel more user-friendly. Oh, and maybe a simple background color. Also, including a message if the form is submitted but no credentials are entered would make it more helpful. Oh right, handling errors here would be good for user experience. So, putting all that together: HTML structure, basic styling, form with input fields, some basic JavaScript for checking credentials, and maybe a message if invalid. That should cover it. Let me draft that out.
</think>

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Login Page</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background-color: #f4f4f9;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .login-container {
      background: white;
      padding: 30px;
      border-radius: 8px;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
      max-width: 300px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      width: 100%;
    }

    .login-form {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .form-group {
      margin-bottom: 15px;
    }

    input[type="text"], input[type="password"] {
      padding: 10px;
      font-size: 16px;
      width: 100%;
      border: 1px solid #ccc;
      border-radius: 4px;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    button {
      padding: 10px 20px;
      font-size: 16px;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 4px;
      cursor: pointer;
      background-color: #3498db;
      color: white;
      border-radius: 4px;
      margin-top: 10px;
    }

    button:hover {
      background-color: #2c9984;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="login-container">
  <h2>Login</h2>
  <form class="login-form">
    <div class="form-group">
      <input type="text" placeholder="Username" required />
    </div>
    <div class="form-group">
      <input type="password" placeholder="Password" required />
    </div>
    <button type="submit">Login</button>
  </form>
  <p style="color:red;">Invalid credentials. Please try again.</p>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

